{
  "video": {
    "id": "MqNq9S1_Ct8",
    "title": "Lipids, Carbohydrates, and Nucleic Acids Practice Problem | MIT 7.01SC Fundamentals of Biology",
    "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MqNq9S1_Ct8",
    "channel": "MIT OpenCourseWare",
    "duration": 513,
    "language": "en"
  },
  "segment_count": 119,
  "segments": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "start": 6.37,
      "end": 8.71,
      "duration": 2.34,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: Hi, my name is Nicole and welcome to"
    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "start": 8.71,
      "end": 10.17,
      "duration": 1.46,
      "text": "recitation."
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "start": 10.17,
      "end": 13.46,
      "duration": 3.29,
      "text": "Today we are going to go over the practice problem for the"
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "start": 13.46,
      "end": 16.79,
      "duration": 3.33,
      "text": "nucleic acids, carbohydrates, and lipids section of the"
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "start": 16.79,
      "end": 18.71,
      "duration": 1.92,
      "text": "biochemistry module."
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "start": 18.71,
      "end": 20.94,
      "duration": 2.23,
      "text": "First, if you haven't had a chance to look at this"
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "start": 20.94,
      "end": 24.86,
      "duration": 3.92,
      "text": "problem, please go back and look at it and then come back"
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "start": 24.86,
      "end": 27.055,
      "duration": 2.195,
      "text": "to recitation and we'll go over it together."
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "start": 33.94,
      "end": 35.04,
      "duration": 1.1,
      "text": "Welcome back."
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "start": 35.04,
      "end": 38.43,
      "duration": 3.39,
      "text": "To start this problem, we are going to go through parts A"
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "start": 38.43,
      "end": 41.68,
      "duration": 3.25,
      "text": "through D and then we'll take a break and come back and do"
    },
    {
      "index": 11,
      "start": 41.68,
      "end": 43.76,
      "duration": 2.08,
      "text": "parts E and F."
    },
    {
      "index": 12,
      "start": 43.76,
      "end": 49.4,
      "duration": 5.64,
      "text": "So, this problem asks us about the molecule shown here."
    },
    {
      "index": 13,
      "start": 49.4,
      "end": 54.05,
      "duration": 4.65,
      "text": "First, we are asked to name this molecule."
    },
    {
      "index": 14,
      "start": 54.05,
      "end": 57.59,
      "duration": 3.54,
      "text": "By looking at this molecule, it's really easy to figure out"
    },
    {
      "index": 15,
      "start": 57.59,
      "end": 58.61,
      "duration": 1.02,
      "text": "what it is."
    },
    {
      "index": 16,
      "start": 58.61,
      "end": 64.15,
      "duration": 5.54,
      "text": "All you have to do is notice the fatty acid tail and the"
    },
    {
      "index": 17,
      "start": 64.15,
      "end": 66.55,
      "duration": 2.4,
      "text": "phosphate head."
    },
    {
      "index": 18,
      "start": 66.55,
      "end": 69.955,
      "duration": 3.405,
      "text": "If you remember from lecture, this should tell you that it"
    },
    {
      "index": 19,
      "start": 69.955,
      "end": 71.205,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "is a phospholipid."
    },
    {
      "index": 20,
      "start": 83.09,
      "end": 87.38,
      "duration": 4.29,
      "text": "Next, we are asked where we find these molecules in living"
    },
    {
      "index": 21,
      "start": 87.38,
      "end": 92.14,
      "duration": 4.76,
      "text": "cells and what the function of these molecules is."
    },
    {
      "index": 22,
      "start": 92.14,
      "end": 96.11,
      "duration": 3.97,
      "text": "So if you remember from lecture, we are told that we"
    },
    {
      "index": 23,
      "start": 96.11,
      "end": 98.685,
      "duration": 2.575,
      "text": "find these molecules in cell membranes."
    },
    {
      "index": 24,
      "start": 109.28,
      "end": 111.97,
      "duration": 2.69,
      "text": "We learned that they are an integral part of cell"
    },
    {
      "index": 25,
      "start": 111.97,
      "end": 116.53,
      "duration": 4.56,
      "text": "membranes and their function is to control the permeability"
    },
    {
      "index": 26,
      "start": 116.53,
      "end": 121.12,
      "duration": 4.59,
      "text": "of the cell, which is a very important function."
    },
    {
      "index": 27,
      "start": 121.12,
      "end": 127.26,
      "duration": 6.14,
      "text": "Their structure allows them to keep out polar molecules and"
    },
    {
      "index": 28,
      "start": 127.26,
      "end": 131.61,
      "duration": 4.35,
      "text": "let in nonpolar molecules so they can allow the cell to"
    },
    {
      "index": 29,
      "start": 131.61,
      "end": 136.32,
      "duration": 4.71,
      "text": "have a high solute concentration on the inside as"
    },
    {
      "index": 30,
      "start": 136.32,
      "end": 138.58,
      "duration": 2.26,
      "text": "compared to the outside."
    },
    {
      "index": 31,
      "start": 138.58,
      "end": 143.84,
      "duration": 5.26,
      "text": "So their critical function is to form a permeability barrier"
    },
    {
      "index": 32,
      "start": 143.84,
      "end": 145.09,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "on the cell."
    },
    {
      "index": 33,
      "start": 158.81,
      "end": 161.23,
      "duration": 2.42,
      "text": "So now that we understand what the function of these"
    },
    {
      "index": 34,
      "start": 161.23,
      "end": 166.5,
      "duration": 5.27,
      "text": "molecules is, this question asks us what would happen if"
    },
    {
      "index": 35,
      "start": 166.5,
      "end": 171.77,
      "duration": 5.27,
      "text": "we dropped these molecules into a glass of water."
    },
    {
      "index": 36,
      "start": 171.77,
      "end": 176.0,
      "duration": 4.23,
      "text": "So sometimes these molecules are drawn like this, with a"
    },
    {
      "index": 37,
      "start": 176.0,
      "end": 179.23,
      "duration": 3.23,
      "text": "circle as the phosphate head and two squiggly"
    },
    {
      "index": 38,
      "start": 179.23,
      "end": 181.14,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "lines as the tail."
    },
    {
      "index": 39,
      "start": 181.14,
      "end": 183.79,
      "duration": 2.65,
      "text": "So if we dropped these in water, we can get three"
    },
    {
      "index": 40,
      "start": 183.79,
      "end": 185.28,
      "duration": 1.49,
      "text": "possibilities."
    },
    {
      "index": 41,
      "start": 185.28,
      "end": 188.93,
      "duration": 3.65,
      "text": "Either they can form a micelle, which is drawn with"
    },
    {
      "index": 42,
      "start": 188.93,
      "end": 192.92,
      "duration": 3.99,
      "text": "all of the heads towards the outside, facing the water"
    },
    {
      "index": 43,
      "start": 192.92,
      "end": 199.05,
      "duration": 6.13,
      "text": "molecules and the tails all hidden on the inside."
    },
    {
      "index": 44,
      "start": 199.05,
      "end": 206.12,
      "duration": 7.07,
      "text": "Or, it can form a liposome, which is two layers with a"
    },
    {
      "index": 45,
      "start": 206.12,
      "end": 211.6,
      "duration": 5.48,
      "text": "very tight layer of phospholipids on the inside"
    },
    {
      "index": 46,
      "start": 211.6,
      "end": 215.24,
      "duration": 3.64,
      "text": "and a larger layer of phospholipids on the outside"
    },
    {
      "index": 47,
      "start": 215.24,
      "end": 222.39,
      "duration": 7.15,
      "text": "with the tails facing inwards and the heads facing outwards"
    },
    {
      "index": 48,
      "start": 222.39,
      "end": 223.64,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "towards the water."
    },
    {
      "index": 49,
      "start": 228.01,
      "end": 232.22,
      "duration": 4.21,
      "text": "And there is also water in the middle as well"
    },
    {
      "index": 50,
      "start": 232.22,
      "end": 233.99,
      "duration": 1.77,
      "text": "facing these nonpolar--"
    },
    {
      "index": 51,
      "start": 233.99,
      "end": 236.44,
      "duration": 2.45,
      "text": "I mean, these polar heads."
    },
    {
      "index": 52,
      "start": 236.44,
      "end": 240.53,
      "duration": 4.09,
      "text": "The third structure they can form is a bilayer."
    },
    {
      "index": 53,
      "start": 240.53,
      "end": 244.05,
      "duration": 3.52,
      "text": "This is a structure that is found that makes cell"
    },
    {
      "index": 54,
      "start": 244.05,
      "end": 247.5,
      "duration": 3.45,
      "text": "membranes, is this phospholipid bilayer."
    },
    {
      "index": 55,
      "start": 247.5,
      "end": 250.115,
      "duration": 2.615,
      "text": "So this is actually a much larger structure--"
    },
    {
      "index": 56,
      "start": 250.115,
      "end": 253.14,
      "duration": 3.025,
      "text": "I've only drawn part of it here--"
    },
    {
      "index": 57,
      "start": 253.14,
      "end": 257.49,
      "duration": 4.35,
      "text": "and this is where you have water on both sides of it."
    },
    {
      "index": 58,
      "start": 257.49,
      "end": 268.18,
      "duration": 10.69,
      "text": "So you have water molecules out here and on the inside of"
    },
    {
      "index": 59,
      "start": 268.18,
      "end": 271.08,
      "duration": 2.9,
      "text": "the bilayer."
    },
    {
      "index": 60,
      "start": 271.08,
      "end": 274.33,
      "duration": 3.25,
      "text": "So those are the three molecules that--"
    },
    {
      "index": 61,
      "start": 274.33,
      "end": 277.46,
      "duration": 3.13,
      "text": "three structures that this molecule will form when you"
    },
    {
      "index": 62,
      "start": 277.46,
      "end": 279.91,
      "duration": 2.45,
      "text": "drop it into water."
    },
    {
      "index": 63,
      "start": 279.91,
      "end": 284.77,
      "duration": 4.86,
      "text": "Now the most important part of this problem is asking why do"
    },
    {
      "index": 64,
      "start": 284.77,
      "end": 286.95,
      "duration": 2.18,
      "text": "these molecules form these structures when"
    },
    {
      "index": 65,
      "start": 286.95,
      "end": 289.15,
      "duration": 2.2,
      "text": "dropped into water."
    },
    {
      "index": 66,
      "start": 289.15,
      "end": 292.35,
      "duration": 3.2,
      "text": "And we can find the answer to this very easily in just"
    },
    {
      "index": 67,
      "start": 292.35,
      "end": 295.37,
      "duration": 3.02,
      "text": "looking at the properties of phospholipids and the"
    },
    {
      "index": 68,
      "start": 295.37,
      "end": 297.27,
      "duration": 1.9,
      "text": "properties of water."
    },
    {
      "index": 69,
      "start": 297.27,
      "end": 301.19,
      "duration": 3.92,
      "text": "If you look at a phospholipid, you'll see that the head, the"
    },
    {
      "index": 70,
      "start": 301.19,
      "end": 305.51,
      "duration": 4.32,
      "text": "phosphate head, is negatively charged, so that means that"
    },
    {
      "index": 71,
      "start": 305.51,
      "end": 315.62,
      "duration": 10.11,
      "text": "it's polar, whereas the tail is a fatty acid, and we have"
    },
    {
      "index": 72,
      "start": 315.62,
      "end": 318.63,
      "duration": 3.01,
      "text": "learned that that means that it is nonpolar,"
    },
    {
      "index": 73,
      "start": 318.63,
      "end": 320.08,
      "duration": 1.45,
      "text": "because it has no charge."
    },
    {
      "index": 74,
      "start": 323.54,
      "end": 325.88,
      "duration": 2.34,
      "text": "And if you look at water, water is a"
    },
    {
      "index": 75,
      "start": 325.88,
      "end": 328.5,
      "duration": 2.62,
      "text": "polar molecule as well."
    },
    {
      "index": 76,
      "start": 328.5,
      "end": 334.11,
      "duration": 5.61,
      "text": "It has two polar bonds to hydrogen."
    },
    {
      "index": 77,
      "start": 334.11,
      "end": 337.89,
      "duration": 3.78,
      "text": "And the reason that they form these structures is because"
    },
    {
      "index": 78,
      "start": 337.89,
      "end": 341.96,
      "duration": 4.07,
      "text": "the polar heads of the phospholipids want to interact"
    },
    {
      "index": 79,
      "start": 341.96,
      "end": 345.53,
      "duration": 3.57,
      "text": "with polar water and the nonpolar tails of the"
    },
    {
      "index": 80,
      "start": 345.53,
      "end": 349.61,
      "duration": 4.08,
      "text": "phospholipids do not want to interact with the polar water."
    },
    {
      "index": 81,
      "start": 349.61,
      "end": 354.04,
      "duration": 4.43,
      "text": "So they have to find the confirmations in which the"
    },
    {
      "index": 82,
      "start": 354.04,
      "end": 356.76,
      "duration": 2.72,
      "text": "tails are hidden from water and the heads"
    },
    {
      "index": 83,
      "start": 356.76,
      "end": 360.17,
      "duration": 3.41,
      "text": "are exposed to water."
    },
    {
      "index": 84,
      "start": 360.17,
      "end": 363.14,
      "duration": 2.97,
      "text": "So now that we understand why phospholipids form these"
    },
    {
      "index": 85,
      "start": 363.14,
      "end": 365.66,
      "duration": 2.52,
      "text": "structures, we're going to take a break and come back to"
    },
    {
      "index": 86,
      "start": 365.66,
      "end": 366.95,
      "duration": 1.29,
      "text": "the second part of the problem."
    },
    {
      "index": 87,
      "start": 370.81,
      "end": 371.63,
      "duration": 0.82,
      "text": "Welcome back."
    },
    {
      "index": 88,
      "start": 371.63,
      "end": 375.4,
      "duration": 3.77,
      "text": "Now we are going to solve parts E and F of this problem."
    },
    {
      "index": 89,
      "start": 375.4,
      "end": 378.72,
      "duration": 3.32,
      "text": "Part E asks us to draw another molecule that contains"
    },
    {
      "index": 90,
      "start": 378.72,
      "end": 383.18,
      "duration": 4.46,
      "text": "phosphate that is essential to biological systems."
    },
    {
      "index": 91,
      "start": 383.18,
      "end": 387.4,
      "duration": 4.22,
      "text": "Right off, you should be thinking about nucleic acids."
    },
    {
      "index": 92,
      "start": 387.4,
      "end": 392.57,
      "duration": 5.17,
      "text": "I have written an example of a nucleic acid up here."
    },
    {
      "index": 93,
      "start": 392.57,
      "end": 399.55,
      "duration": 6.98,
      "text": "This, as you can see by the A in the base position, is ATP."
    },
    {
      "index": 94,
      "start": 399.55,
      "end": 402.88,
      "duration": 3.33,
      "text": "And you can see where phosphate is essential as the"
    },
    {
      "index": 95,
      "start": 402.88,
      "end": 407.74,
      "duration": 4.86,
      "text": "triphosphate portion of ATP."
    },
    {
      "index": 96,
      "start": 407.74,
      "end": 411.56,
      "duration": 3.82,
      "text": "The next part of the question asks us what is the function"
    },
    {
      "index": 97,
      "start": 411.56,
      "end": 413.8,
      "duration": 2.24,
      "text": "of these type of molecules?"
    },
    {
      "index": 98,
      "start": 413.8,
      "end": 417.64,
      "duration": 3.84,
      "text": "So the molecule that I chose to draw, ATP, is very"
    },
    {
      "index": 99,
      "start": 417.64,
      "end": 421.12,
      "duration": 3.48,
      "text": "interesting because it has multiple functions."
    },
    {
      "index": 100,
      "start": 421.12,
      "end": 428.72,
      "duration": 7.6,
      "text": "It serves as a building block of RNA through oligomerization"
    },
    {
      "index": 101,
      "start": 428.72,
      "end": 432.12,
      "duration": 3.4,
      "text": "through this bond by adding multiple"
    },
    {
      "index": 102,
      "start": 432.12,
      "end": 433.505,
      "duration": 1.385,
      "text": "nucleic acids together."
    },
    {
      "index": 103,
      "start": 438.85,
      "end": 444.01,
      "duration": 5.16,
      "text": "It also serves as an energy source for the cell, the"
    },
    {
      "index": 104,
      "start": 444.01,
      "end": 452.98,
      "duration": 8.97,
      "text": "energy source for the cell, through breaking of this bond,"
    },
    {
      "index": 105,
      "start": 452.98,
      "end": 456.56,
      "duration": 3.58,
      "text": "which is an exergonic reaction and releases energy and allows"
    },
    {
      "index": 106,
      "start": 456.56,
      "end": 460.16,
      "duration": 3.6,
      "text": "a lot of the processes in the cell that wouldn't normally be"
    },
    {
      "index": 107,
      "start": 460.16,
      "end": 462.53,
      "duration": 2.37,
      "text": "able to occur to occur."
    },
    {
      "index": 108,
      "start": 462.53,
      "end": 467.01,
      "duration": 4.48,
      "text": "So I'm going to put as a function of this molecule as"
    },
    {
      "index": 109,
      "start": 467.01,
      "end": 477.24,
      "duration": 10.23,
      "text": "both energy and RNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 110,
      "start": 480.74,
      "end": 484.69,
      "duration": 3.95,
      "text": "So now that we understand the properties of phospholipids"
    },
    {
      "index": 111,
      "start": 484.69,
      "end": 488.07,
      "duration": 3.38,
      "text": "and we've been able to identify another very"
    },
    {
      "index": 112,
      "start": 488.07,
      "end": 492.31,
      "duration": 4.24,
      "text": "important molecule that contains phosphate, we can"
    },
    {
      "index": 113,
      "start": 492.31,
      "end": 495.09,
      "duration": 2.78,
      "text": "move on to the rest of the biochemistry section."
    },
    {
      "index": 114,
      "start": 497.68,
      "end": 500.56,
      "duration": 2.88,
      "text": "In this problem, we have learned about the properties"
    },
    {
      "index": 115,
      "start": 500.56,
      "end": 504.6,
      "duration": 4.04,
      "text": "of phospholipids as well as the importance of phosphate in"
    },
    {
      "index": 116,
      "start": 504.6,
      "end": 506.51,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "nucleic acids."
    },
    {
      "index": 117,
      "start": 506.51,
      "end": 510.05,
      "duration": 3.54,
      "text": "I hope you've enjoyed watching this video and I hope to see"
    },
    {
      "index": 118,
      "start": 510.05,
      "end": 511.3,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "you next time."
    }
  ],
  "course": {
    "category": "Biology & Chemistry",
    "title": "Introduction to Biology",
